  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-12), V.F.X grip [No Twist] seen from the left-front: head with the mode drum (SW/GUN marks, red selector lever) on the left, POV hat and red button on top, red trigger under the head, side plate with the wheel on top and a grey button, brake lever at the front, small red button above the lever pivot, knurled grip nut at the bottom",
  "mappingSource": "catalog sources: Virpil support \"VPC V.F.X Grip\" control sheet (https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001250821-vpc-v-f-x-grip, attachment 47246733476, the twist version; same controls otherwise per https://virpil-controls.eu/vpc-vfx-grip-nt.html). Traced on that sheet: 11 + U/L/R/D POV hat, 5 red button beside it, 2 and 7/8/9/10 the mode drum selector, 14 / D / 12 the side wheel, 16 the side-plate button, 1/6 trigger, 3 front button above the lever, 4 / S the lever, 15 / Z / 13 the twist ring at the grip base",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "positions are placed on this NT product photo by matching the sheet drawing (same view). The catalog's \"Pinky button\" (BTN4) is the lever's end click on the sheet (box 4 grouped with S, like 31/S on the ALPHA); numbers agree, marker on the lever. REPORT: the catalog keeps the two \"Twist-end buttons\" 13 and 15 for this No-Twist variant; on the sheet they share one box group with the twist axis Z at the twist ring, which this variant does not have, so they are probably absent on the NT grip (not placed). Mode drum: 2 (one dot) and 7-10 are drawn on the same selector lever; which of 7-10 is which drum position (SP/PH, SW, GUN, OFF) is not drawn.",
